> Module Elderly_and_disabled

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Credit for the elderly or the disabled (Schedule R)

Direct File module `elderlyAndDisabled.xml`
(`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/elderlyAndDisabled.xml`,
"DF" below, 1810 lines), scope.md section 6.5, issue #30. Tests:
`catala/tests/test_elderly_and_disabled.catala_en`. Oracle comparison:
`difftest/mappings/elderly_and_disabled.mjs`
(`make difftest SCOPE=elderly_and_disabled`).

Law and forms (all under `sources/`): IRC 22 (`statute/irc-22.html`), Schedule R
(`forms-instructions/f1040sr--2024.pdf` pp 1-2) and its instructions
(`forms-instructions/i1040sr--2024.pdf` pp R-1 to R-7).

The credit is non-refundable, so it is limited by the tax left after the credits
applied before it (CONVENTIONS.md section 7, stage 5: CDCC first, then Schedule
R). That remaining tax is the input `credit_limit_worksheet_line_3`, filled by
the 1040 wiring step. Inputs follow CONVENTIONS.md section 3 (complete).

Scope limits: the physician's statement (Schedule R Part II) changes no number,
and DF takes it as answers kept for the return records, so it is not modelled.
Nonresident aliens are knocked out elsewhere (IRC 22(f)). This module has no
knockout of its own: DF's `elderlyAndDisabled.xml` defines none.

**Direct File bug found, `DF-BUG(13)`** (number tentative, see the PR): DF adds the
nontaxable part of pensions and annuities on 1040 line 5a minus line 5b
(`income.xml` `/nonTaxablePensionsAndAnnuities`) to Schedule R line 13b. The
statute and the instructions exclude it. See line 13b below.

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## Answers about disability for one filer. DF asks these only of a filer under
## 65 (and of the secondary filer only on a joint return); the caller sends
## the answers anyway and the rules ignore them when they do not apply.
declaration structure DisabilityAnswers:
  # DF: /filers/*/isRetOnPermOrTotalDisability
  data is_retired_on_perm_or_total_disability content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/employerHasMandatoryRetirementAge
  data employer_has_mandatory_retirement_age content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/hasMetEmployerMandatoryRetirementAge
  data has_met_employer_mandatory_retirement_age content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/arePaymentsTaxDisabilityIncome
  data are_payments_taxable_disability_income content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/writableTotalTaxableDisabilityAmount
  data writable_total_taxable_disability_amount content money
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerHasW2WagesGreaterThan0 or
  # /secondaryFilerHasW2WagesGreaterThan0 (wages > 0 for this filer)
  data has_w2_wages content boolean

## One filer's disability facts. Called once for each filer.
declaration scope EdcFiler:
  # DF: /filers/*/isPrimaryFilerOrMfjAndEither
  input counts_for_return condition
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled
  input maybe_eligible_for_credit condition
  # DF: /filers/*/age65OrOlder (filers.xml)
  input age65_or_older condition
  input answers content DisabilityAnswers

  # DF: /filers/*/hasDisabilityIncome
  output has_disability_income condition
  # DF: /filers/*/hasTaxableDisabilityPaymentsAndRetOnDisability
  output has_taxable_disability_payments condition
  # DF: /filers/*/totalTaxableDisabilityAmount
  output total_taxable_disability_amount content money
  # DF: /filers/*/isMaybeQualifiedforEdcThroughDisability
  output is_qualified_through_disability condition

## Schedule R for the return.
declaration scope ScheduleR:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: filers.xml /livedApartAllYear (only read for MFS)
  input lived_apart_all_year condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  input primary_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/age65OrOlder (read only on a joint return)
  input secondary_age65_or_older condition
  input primary_answers content DisabilityAnswers
  input secondary_answers content DisabilityAnswers
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /agi, Form 1040 line 11 (Schedule R line 14)
  input agi content money
  # DF: socialSecurity.xml /nonTaxableSocialSecurityBenefits (Social_security
  # scope output non_taxable_benefits), Schedule R line 13a
  input non_taxable_social_security_benefits content money
  # DF: /edcSelfReportedNonTaxablePaymentAmount, line 13b: nontaxable
  # veterans' pensions and other benefits excluded under non-Code law, as the
  # filer reports them (DF gates it on its own yes/no question, then rounds)
  input self_reported_non_taxable_payments content money
  # Credit Limit Worksheet line 3 (i1040sr--2024.pdf p R-5): Form 1040 line 18
  # minus Schedule 3 lines 1, 2 and 6l. DF: /edcTaxLiabilityLimitCalc
  input credit_limit_worksheet_line_3 content money

  primary scope EdcFiler
  secondary scope EdcFiler

  # DF: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFJ (derived from filing_status)
  internal is_mfj condition
  internal is_mfs condition
  internal is_single_hoh_qss condition
  # The two filers' ages, with the secondary one counted only when joint
  internal primary_is_65 condition
  internal secondary_is_65 condition
  # DF: /filersQualifiedForEdcThroughDisability, as a count
  internal number_qualified_through_disability content integer
  # DF: /mfjAndOnlyOneQualfiedForEdc
  internal mfj_and_only_one_qualified condition
  # DF: /edcRelaxedAgiLimit
  internal relaxed_agi_limit content money
  # DF: /edcRelaxedNontaxableLimit
  internal relaxed_non_taxable_limit content money
  # DF: /atLeastOneTpIsUnder65 (filers.xml)
  internal at_least_one_tp_is_under_65 condition
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled
  internal maybe_eligible_for_credit condition

  # Part I boxes. DF: /edcLine1 ... /edcLine9
  output edc_line1 condition
  output edc_line2 condition
  output edc_line3 condition
  output edc_line4 condition
  output edc_line5 condition
  output edc_line6 condition
  output edc_line7 condition
  output edc_line8 condition
  output edc_line9 condition

  # Part III
  # DF: /edcFilingStatusAmt, line 10
  output edc_filing_status_amt content money
  # DF: /statusBasedDisabilityIncome, line 11
  output status_based_disability_income content money
  # DF: /lesserOfFilingStatusAmountAndTaxableDisabilityIncome, line 12
  output lesser_of_filing_status_amount_and_taxable_disability_income content money
  # DF: /edcNonTaxableSocialSecurityAndRailroadBenefits, line 13a
  output edc_non_taxable_social_security_and_railroad_benefits content money
  # DF: /edcNonTaxableIncomeNotIncludingSocialSecurityAndRrb, line 13b
  output edc_non_taxable_income_not_including_social_security_and_rrb content money
  # DF: /edcTotalNonTaxableAmount, line 13c
  output edc_total_non_taxable_amount content money
  # DF: /edcExemptionAmount, line 15 (no box checked: $0, DF leaves it unset)
  output edc_exemption_amount content money
  # DF: /edcMagi, line 16
  output edc_magi content money
  # DF: /edcHalfMagi, line 17
  output edc_half_magi content money
  # DF: /edcAdjustedCreditAmount, line 18
  output edc_adjusted_credit_amount content money
  # DF: /edcNetCreditAmount, line 19
  output edc_net_credit_amount content money
  # DF: /netEdcAmount, line 20
  output net_edc_amount content money
  # DF: /edcTaxLiabilityLimit, line 21
  output edc_tax_liability_limit content money
  # DF: /totalEdc, line 22: Schedule 3 line 6d
  output total_edc content money

  # Eligibility. DF: /edcAgiLimitBasedOnQualified
  output edc_agi_limit content money
  # DF: /edcNonTaxableLimitBasedOnQualified
  output edc_non_taxable_limit content money
  # DF: /isQualifiedForEdcBasedOnAgeOrDisability
  output is_qualified_based_on_age_or_disability condition
  # DF: /qualifiedForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled
  output qualified_for_credit_for_elderly_and_disabled condition
  # DF: /isReceivingEdc
  output is_receiving_edc condition
```

## IRC 22(b): qualified individual, disability limb

"(b) ... the term 'qualified individual' means any individual— (1) who has
attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year, or (2) who retired on
disability before the close of the taxable year and who, when he retired, was
permanently and totally disabled."

The instructions add what the form needs (`i1040sr--2024.pdf` p R-1): a filer
under 65 "can qualify for the credit only if you are retired on permanent and
total disability, have taxable disability income, and as of January 1, 2024,
had not reached mandatory retirement age". "Disability income must ... be
included in your income as wages (or payments instead of wages) for the time you
are absent from work" (p R-3). DF can only hold such income in a W-2, so it asks
about disability only of a filer with W-2 wages above zero (`/filers/*/
maybeEligibleForDisabilityCredit`), reproduced by `has_w2_wages`. That is a
limit of what the return can contain, not a different reading of the law.

```catala
scope EdcFiler:
  # IRC 22(b)(2); i1040sr--2024.pdf p R-1, R-3.
  # DF: elderlyAndDisabled.xml /filers/*/hasDisabilityIncome
  # (DF asks the disability questions only when the credit may apply at all:
  # `/filers/*/maybeEligibleForDisabilityCredit` includes the "maybe eligible"
  # fact, so the boxes below stay unchecked for a return with no tax to offset.)
  definition has_disability_income equals
    counts_for_return
    and maybe_eligible_for_credit
    and (not age65_or_older)
    and answers.has_w2_wages
    and answers.is_retired_on_perm_or_total_disability
    and ((not answers.employer_has_mandatory_retirement_age)
         or (not answers.has_met_employer_mandatory_retirement_age))

  # DF: /filers/*/hasTaxableDisabilityPaymentsAndRetOnDisability
  definition has_taxable_disability_payments equals
    has_disability_income and answers.are_payments_taxable_disability_income

  # IRC 22(c)(2)(B)(iii): "disability income". DF: /filers/*/totalTaxableDisabilityAmount
  definition total_taxable_disability_amount equals
    if has_taxable_disability_payments
    then answers.writable_total_taxable_disability_amount
    else $0

  # DF: /filers/*/isMaybeQualifiedforEdcThroughDisability: the filer has
  # taxable disability income, which must be more than zero
  definition is_qualified_through_disability equals
    has_taxable_disability_payments and total_taxable_disability_amount != $0
```

## Part I: the box for filing status and age

Schedule R Part I (`f1040sr--2024.pdf` p 1): Single, head of household or
qualifying surviving spouse: box 1 "You were 65 or older", box 2 "You were under
65 and you retired on permanent and total disability". Married filing jointly:
box 3 both spouses 65 or older; box 4 both under 65, only one retired on
permanent and total disability; box 5 both under 65, both retired on disability;
box 6 one spouse 65 or older, the other under 65 and retired on disability; box 7
one spouse 65 or older, the other under 65 and not retired on disability.
Married filing separately: box 8 "65 or older and you lived apart from your
spouse for all of 2024", box 9 "under 65, retired on permanent and total
disability, and you lived apart from your spouse for all of 2024".

IRC 22(e)(1): "Except in the case of a husband and wife who live apart at all
times during the taxable year, if the taxpayer is married at the close of the
taxable year, the credit provided by this section shall be allowed only if the
taxpayer and his spouse file a joint return for the taxable year." A married
filer filing separately and not living apart therefore gets no credit; this
module checks that in the eligibility rules, as DF does in
`/maybeEligibleForCreditForElderlyAndDisabledWoTaxLiability`.

```catala
scope ScheduleR:
  definition is_mfj equals filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
  definition is_mfs equals filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition is_single_hoh_qss equals
    not (is_mfj or is_mfs)

  definition primary.counts_for_return equals true
  definition primary.maybe_eligible_for_credit equals maybe_eligible_for_credit
  definition secondary.maybe_eligible_for_credit equals maybe_eligible_for_credit
  definition primary.age65_or_older equals primary_age65_or_older
  definition primary.answers equals primary_answers
  definition secondary.counts_for_return equals is_mfj
  definition secondary.age65_or_older equals secondary_age65_or_older
  definition secondary.answers equals secondary_answers

  # DF: /primaryFiler/age65OrOlder, /secondaryFiler/age65OrOlder; the
  # secondary filer exists only on a joint return
  definition primary_is_65 equals primary_age65_or_older
  definition secondary_is_65 equals is_mfj and secondary_age65_or_older

  # DF: CollectionSize of /filersQualifiedForEdcThroughDisability
  definition number_qualified_through_disability equals
    (if primary.is_qualified_through_disability then 1 else 0)
    + (if secondary.is_qualified_through_disability then 1 else 0)

  # DF: /edcLine1
  definition edc_line1 equals is_single_hoh_qss and primary_is_65
  # DF: /edcLine2
  definition edc_line2 equals
    is_single_hoh_qss and primary.is_qualified_through_disability
  # DF: /edcLine3
  definition edc_line3 equals is_mfj and primary_is_65 and secondary_is_65
  # DF: /edcLine4
  definition edc_line4 equals
    is_mfj and (not primary_is_65) and (not secondary_is_65)
    and number_qualified_through_disability = 1
  # DF: /edcLine5
  definition edc_line5 equals
    is_mfj and (not primary_is_65) and (not secondary_is_65)
    and number_qualified_through_disability = 2
  # DF: /edcLine6. One spouse is 65 or older, the other is under 65 and retired
  # on disability with taxable disability income
  definition edc_line6 equals
    is_mfj and
    ((primary_is_65 and (not secondary_is_65)
      and secondary.is_qualified_through_disability)
     or (secondary_is_65 and (not primary_is_65)
         and primary.is_qualified_through_disability))
  # DF: /edcLine7. One spouse is 65 or older, the other is under 65 and not
  # retired on disability
  definition edc_line7 equals
    is_mfj and
    ((primary_is_65 and (not secondary_is_65)
      and (not secondary.is_qualified_through_disability))
     or (secondary_is_65 and (not primary_is_65)
         and (not primary.is_qualified_through_disability)))
  # DF: /edcLine8
  definition edc_line8 equals is_mfs and primary_is_65
  # DF: /edcLine9
  definition edc_line9 equals
    is_mfs and (not primary_is_65) and primary.is_qualified_through_disability
```

## IRC 22(c)(2): initial amount, Schedule R lines 10 to 12

"(2) Initial amount (A) In general Except as provided in subparagraph (B), the
initial amount shall be— (i) $5,000 in the case of a single individual, or a
joint return where only one spouse is a qualified individual, (ii) $7,500 in
the case of a joint return where both spouses are qualified individuals, or
(iii) $3,750 in the case of a married individual filing a separate return."

"(B) ... (i) In the case of a qualified individual who has not attained age 65
before the close of the taxable year ... the initial amount shall not exceed the
disability income for the taxable year. (ii) ... (I) if both spouses have not
attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year, the initial amount shall
not exceed the sum of such spouses' disability income, or (II) if one spouse has
attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year, the initial amount shall
not exceed the sum of $5,000 plus the disability income for the taxable year of
the spouse who has not attained age 65."

Schedule R line 10 (`f1040sr--2024.pdf` p 2): box 1, 2, 4 or 7 $5,000; box 3, 5
or 6 $7,500; box 8 or 9 $3,750. Line 11: box 6, "$5,000 to the taxable
disability income of the spouse who was under age 65"; box 2, 4 or 9 "your
taxable disability income"; box 5, "your taxable disability income to your
spouse's". Line 12: "If you completed line 11, enter the smaller of line 10 or
line 11. All others, enter the amount from line 10."

```catala
scope ScheduleR:
  # Schedule R line 10. DF: /edcFilingStatusAmt ($0 when no box is checked)
  definition edc_filing_status_amt equals
    if edc_line1 or edc_line2 or edc_line4 or edc_line7
    then P.edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified
    else if edc_line3 or edc_line5 or edc_line6
    then P.edc_initial_amount_joint_both_qualified
    else if edc_line8 or edc_line9
    then P.edc_initial_amount_married_separate
    else $0

  # Schedule R line 11. DF: /statusBasedDisabilityIncome
  definition status_based_disability_income equals
    if edc_line6 then
      (if primary.is_qualified_through_disability
       then primary.total_taxable_disability_amount + P.edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified
       else secondary.total_taxable_disability_amount + P.edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified)
    else if edc_line2 or edc_line9 then primary.total_taxable_disability_amount
    else if edc_line4 then
      (if primary.is_qualified_through_disability
       then primary.total_taxable_disability_amount
       else secondary.total_taxable_disability_amount)
    else if edc_line5 then
      primary.total_taxable_disability_amount + secondary.total_taxable_disability_amount
    else $0

  # Schedule R line 12. DF: /lesserOfFilingStatusAmountAndTaxableDisabilityIncome
  definition lesser_of_filing_status_amount_and_taxable_disability_income equals
    if number_qualified_through_disability > 0
    then Money.min of edc_filing_status_amt, status_based_disability_income
    else edc_filing_status_amt
```

## IRC 22(c)(3): reduction for nontaxable pensions, Schedule R line 13

"(3) Reduction (A) In general The reduction under this paragraph is an amount
equal to the sum of the amounts received by the individual (or, in the case of a
joint return, by either spouse) as a pension or annuity or as a disability
benefit— (i) which is excluded from gross income and payable under— (I) title II
of the Social Security Act, (II) the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974, or (III) a
law administered by the Department of Veterans Affairs, or (ii) which is
excluded from gross income under any provision of law not contained in this
title."

Line 13a is the nontaxable social security (and tier 1 railroad) benefits, "the
difference between the amounts entered on Form 1040 or 1040-SR, line 6a and line
6b" (`i1040sr--2024.pdf` p R-4). Line 13b: "Veterans' pensions (but not military
disability pensions)" and "Any other pension, annuity, or disability benefit that
is excluded from income under any provision of federal law other than the
Internal Revenue Code. Don't include amounts that are treated as a return of your
cost of a pension or annuity" (p R-5). Line 13c "Add lines 13a and 13b".

`DF-BUG(13)`: DF line 13b is `/edcSelfReportedNonTaxablePaymentAmount` plus
`/nonTaxablePensionsAndAnnuities`, which is 1040 line 5a minus line 5b
(`income.xml` line 652, `elderlyAndDisabled.xml` fact
`/edcNonTaxableIncomeNotIncludingSocialSecurityAndRrb`). Within Direct File's
supported 1099-R codes (2, 7, G, H) that difference is a return of the filer's
cost (excluded by IRC 72, "contained in this title") or a direct rollover (IRC
402(c), also "this title"). Both are outside IRC 22(c)(3)(A) and are excluded by
the sentence quoted from the instructions. DF over-reduces the credit. We follow
the statute: line 13b is the self-reported figure only. The difftest mapping
lists the 1040-line-5 scenarios as a known divergence.

```catala
scope ScheduleR:
  # Schedule R line 13a; IRC 22(c)(3)(A)(i). DF: /edcNonTaxableSocialSecurityAndRailroadBenefits
  definition edc_non_taxable_social_security_and_railroad_benefits equals
    non_taxable_social_security_benefits

  # Schedule R line 13b; IRC 22(c)(3)(A)(i)(III), (ii).
  # DF-BUG(13): DF also adds 1040 line 5a - line 5b (cost recovery and rollovers
  # under Code sections 72 and 402). The law excludes them, so we do not.
  # DF: /edcNonTaxableIncomeNotIncludingSocialSecurityAndRrb
  definition edc_non_taxable_income_not_including_social_security_and_rrb equals
    self_reported_non_taxable_payments

  # Schedule R line 13c. DF: /edcTotalNonTaxableAmount (Round, floor at $0)
  definition edc_total_non_taxable_amount equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.positive of
      (edc_non_taxable_social_security_and_railroad_benefits
       + edc_non_taxable_income_not_including_social_security_and_rrb))
```

## IRC 22(d): adjusted gross income limitation, lines 14 to 18

"(d) ... If the adjusted gross income of the taxpayer exceeds— (1) $7,500 in the
case of a single individual, (2) $10,000 in the case of a joint return, or (3)
$5,000 in the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the section
22 amount shall be reduced by one-half of the excess of the adjusted gross income
over $7,500, $10,000, or $5,000, as the case may be."

Schedule R lines 15 to 18 (`f1040sr--2024.pdf` p 2): line 15 is $7,500 for box 1
or 2, $10,000 for box 3, 4, 5, 6 or 7, $5,000 for box 8 or 9. Line 16 "Subtract
line 15 from line 14. If zero or less, enter -0-"; line 17 "one-half of line 16";
line 18 "Add lines 13c and 17". DF rounds the result of lines 16 and 17
(`/edcMagi`, `/edcHalfMagi`), and the 1040 instructions round to whole dollars,
so a half dollar rounds up.

```catala
scope ScheduleR:
  # Schedule R line 15. DF: /edcExemptionAmount
  definition edc_exemption_amount equals
    if edc_line8 or edc_line9 then P.edc_agi_threshold_married_separate
    else if edc_line1 or edc_line2 then P.edc_agi_threshold_single
    else if edc_line3 or edc_line4 or edc_line5 or edc_line6 or edc_line7
    then P.edc_agi_threshold_joint
    else $0

  # Schedule R line 16. DF: /edcMagi
  definition edc_magi equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.positive of (agi - edc_exemption_amount))

  # Schedule R line 17. DF: /edcHalfMagi
  definition edc_half_magi equals
    R.round_dollar of (edc_magi * P.edc_agi_reduction_rate)

  # Schedule R line 18. DF: /edcAdjustedCreditAmount
  definition edc_adjusted_credit_amount equals
    edc_total_non_taxable_amount + edc_half_magi
```

## IRC 22(a): the credit, lines 19 to 22

"(a) General rule In the case of a qualified individual, there shall be allowed as
a credit against the tax imposed by this chapter for the taxable year an amount
equal to 15 percent of such individual's section 22 amount for such taxable
year."

Line 19: "Subtract line 18 from line 12. If zero or less, stop; you can't take the
credit." Line 20: "Multiply line 19 by 15% (0.15)." Line 21: the Credit Limit
Worksheet (`i1040sr--2024.pdf` p R-5): "1. Enter the amount from Form 1040 or
1040-SR, line 18. 2. Enter the amount from Schedule 3 (Form 1040), lines 1, 2,
and 6l. 3. Subtract line 2 from line 1. Enter this amount on Schedule R (Form
1040), line 21. But if zero or less, STOP; you can't take this credit." Line 22:
"Enter the smaller of line 20 or line 21."

DF does the 15% step in `/netEdcAmount` (the fact the survey missed): `Round`
of line 19 times 15/100, to the whole dollar (ties up). Example from the
instructions, Jesse (p R-5): line 19 is $500, line 20 is $75, limit $51, credit
$51.

```catala
scope ScheduleR:
  # Schedule R line 19. DF: /edcNetCreditAmount (and /hasEdcNetCreditAmount)
  definition edc_net_credit_amount equals
    Money.positive of
      (lesser_of_filing_status_amount_and_taxable_disability_income
       - edc_adjusted_credit_amount)

  # Schedule R line 20. DF: /netEdcAmount
  definition net_edc_amount equals
    R.round_dollar of (edc_net_credit_amount * P.edc_credit_rate)

  # Schedule R line 21. DF: /edcTaxLiabilityLimit
  definition edc_tax_liability_limit equals
    Money.positive of credit_limit_worksheet_line_3
```

## Who may take the credit

Table 1 of the instructions (`i1040sr--2024.pdf` p R-7): "you generally CAN'T take
the credit if" Form 1040 line 11 is "$17,500 or more" (single, head of household,
qualifying surviving spouse), "$20,000 or more" (joint, only one spouse is a
qualified individual), "$25,000 or more" (joint, both are), "$12,500 or more"
(married filing separately and lived apart all year), "OR the total of your
nontaxable social security and other nontaxable pension(s) ... is equal to or more
than" $5,000, $5,000, $7,500 and $3,750 respectively. Both tests are strict
(`<`), as in DF `/isQualifiedForEdcBasedOnAgiLimit` and
`/isQualifiedForEdcBasedOnNonTaxablePayments`.

DF's `/qualifiedForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled` is the conjunction of: tax
liability above zero, `/maybeEligibleForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled` (a first
screen that DF applies before it asks the disability questions: the "relaxed"
AGI and nontaxable limits that hold whether or not both spouses qualify, the
married-filing-separately living-apart rule, and age 65 or W-2 wages), the age or
disability test, the exact AGI limit and the exact nontaxable limit with a
positive line 19. The screen never rejects anything the exact tests accept, so it
changes no credit; it does decide whether the Part I boxes for a disabled filer are
checked, which the oracle exposes, so it is reproduced.

```catala
scope ScheduleR:
  definition relaxed_agi_limit equals
    if is_mfj then P.edc_agi_limit_joint_both_qualified
    else if is_mfs then P.edc_agi_limit_married_separate
    else P.edc_agi_limit_single_hoh_qss
  definition relaxed_non_taxable_limit equals
    if is_mfj then P.edc_initial_amount_joint_both_qualified
    else if is_mfs then P.edc_initial_amount_married_separate
    else P.edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified
  definition at_least_one_tp_is_under_65 equals
    if is_mfj then (not primary_age65_or_older) or (not secondary_age65_or_older)
    else not primary_age65_or_older

  # DF: /maybeEligibleForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled and ...WoTaxLiability.
  # Total W-2 wages above zero is "some filer has W-2 wages" (DF /wages > 0).
  definition maybe_eligible_for_credit equals
    credit_limit_worksheet_line_3 > $0
    and (primary_is_65 or secondary_is_65
         or (at_least_one_tp_is_under_65
             and (primary_answers.has_w2_wages or secondary_answers.has_w2_wages)))
    and agi < relaxed_agi_limit
    and non_taxable_social_security_benefits < relaxed_non_taxable_limit
    and ((not is_mfs) or lived_apart_all_year)

  # DF: /filersQualifiedForEdcThroughDisability plus /atLeastOneTpIs65OrOlder
  definition is_qualified_based_on_age_or_disability equals
    primary_is_65 or secondary_is_65 or number_qualified_through_disability > 0

  # DF: /mfjAndOnlyOneQualfiedForEdc: exactly one spouse is 65 or older or
  # qualifies through disability
  definition mfj_and_only_one_qualified equals
    is_mfj
    and ((if primary_is_65 or primary.is_qualified_through_disability then 1 else 0)
         + (if secondary_is_65 or secondary.is_qualified_through_disability then 1 else 0)) = 1

  # Table 1, AGI column. DF: /edcAgiLimitBasedOnQualified
  definition edc_agi_limit equals
    if mfj_and_only_one_qualified then P.edc_agi_limit_joint_one_qualified
    else if is_mfj then P.edc_agi_limit_joint_both_qualified
    else if is_mfs then P.edc_agi_limit_married_separate
    else P.edc_agi_limit_single_hoh_qss

  # Table 1, nontaxable column. DF: /edcNonTaxableLimitBasedOnQualified
  definition edc_non_taxable_limit equals
    if mfj_and_only_one_qualified then P.edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified
    else if is_mfj then P.edc_initial_amount_joint_both_qualified
    else if is_mfs then P.edc_initial_amount_married_separate
    else P.edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified

  # IRC 22(e)(1); DF: /qualifiedForCreditForElderlyAndDisabled
  definition qualified_for_credit_for_elderly_and_disabled equals
    edc_tax_liability_limit > $0
    and maybe_eligible_for_credit
    and is_qualified_based_on_age_or_disability
    and agi < edc_agi_limit
    and edc_net_credit_amount > $0
    and edc_total_non_taxable_amount < edc_non_taxable_limit

  # Schedule R line 22; Schedule 3 line 6d. DF: /totalEdc
  definition total_edc equals
    if qualified_for_credit_for_elderly_and_disabled
    then Money.min of net_edc_amount, edc_tax_liability_limit
    else $0

  # DF: /isReceivingEdc
  definition is_receiving_edc equals
    qualified_for_credit_for_elderly_and_disabled and total_edc > $0
```
